1
00:00:02,180 --> 00:00:05,100
=The Truth (Season 4)=
(Behind-the-Scenes Cast Interview)

2
00:00:05,440 --> 00:00:08,650
(Sun Leyan as Yan Reason)
From host to mystery-show swordswoman,

3
00:00:08,650 --> 00:00:11,180
what's been the biggest challenge?

4
00:00:12,120 --> 00:00:14,550
Everything's been challenging,

5
00:00:14,560 --> 00:00:16,149
but it's also really exciting.

6
00:00:16,160 --> 00:00:18,430
I've always wanted

7
00:00:18,440 --> 00:00:20,350
to play a swordswoman

8
00:00:20,360 --> 00:00:22,270
like this.

9
00:00:22,280 --> 00:00:22,950
And this time,

10
00:00:22,960 --> 00:00:24,430
I got to try

11
00:00:24,440 --> 00:00:26,790
long scenes and fight sequences
for the first time.

12
00:00:26,800 --> 00:00:28,790
Especially when I trained

13
00:00:28,800 --> 00:00:30,230
with the two stunt instructors,

14
00:00:30,240 --> 00:00:33,230
everything felt completely new.

15
00:00:33,240 --> 00:00:34,700
(New experience +1)
And

16
00:00:34,700 --> 00:00:37,030
I picked it up pretty fast.

17
00:00:37,040 --> 00:00:39,870
So especially with the fight moves,

18
00:00:39,880 --> 00:00:40,590
it was

19
00:00:40,600 --> 00:00:41,590
a totally different experience.

20
00:00:42,240 --> 00:00:43,520
How was the team you imagined

21
00:00:43,520 --> 00:00:45,460
different from meeting them today?

22
00:00:45,880 --> 00:00:47,830
I'd met them before

23
00:00:47,840 --> 00:00:49,830
when I was hosting,

24
00:00:49,840 --> 00:00:51,830
so my first

25
00:00:51,840 --> 00:00:53,830
impression was how warm they were.

26
00:00:53,840 --> 00:00:54,670
It felt like one big family

27
00:00:54,680 --> 00:00:56,430
coming to welcome you.

28
00:00:56,440 --> 00:00:58,230
And secondly, I could tell

29
00:00:58,240 --> 00:01:00,790
they were seriously hot.

30
00:01:00,800 --> 00:01:02,830
It was insanely hot today.

31
00:01:02,840 --> 00:01:03,270
And

32
00:01:03,280 --> 00:01:05,750
when we filmed that part,

33
00:01:05,760 --> 00:01:06,910
the sun was beating down.

34
00:01:06,920 --> 00:01:08,910
It was probably the hottest

35
00:01:08,920 --> 00:01:09,710
time of the day.

36
00:01:09,720 --> 00:01:12,190
Everyone was sweating nonstop,

37
00:01:12,200 --> 00:01:14,310
but nobody complained

38
00:01:14,320 --> 00:01:16,270
or asked

39
00:01:16,280 --> 00:01:17,350
for special treatment.

40
00:01:17,360 --> 00:01:18,190
Everyone

41
00:01:18,200 --> 00:01:20,790
was totally absorbed
in solving the mystery.

42
00:01:20,800 --> 00:01:23,150
That pulled me in too.

43
00:01:23,160 --> 00:01:23,830
I got completely

44
00:01:23,840 --> 00:01:25,390
swept up in the story.

45
00:01:25,400 --> 00:01:26,870
So I kept

46
00:01:26,880 --> 00:01:28,910
reminding myself

47
00:01:28,920 --> 00:01:30,670
that I was Yan Reason, the swordswoman,

48
00:01:30,680 --> 00:01:32,950
and kept giving them clues and help.

49
00:01:33,840 --> 00:01:35,110
In the story,

50
00:01:35,120 --> 00:01:35,790
you and Jin Jing's character,

51
00:01:35,800 --> 00:01:37,390
Jin Thrifty...

52
00:01:37,400 --> 00:01:38,230
We're best friends.

53
00:01:38,380 --> 00:01:39,690
How did it feel

54
00:01:39,690 --> 00:01:41,100
interacting with Jin Jing?

55
00:01:41,440 --> 00:01:42,350
Really natural.

56
00:01:42,360 --> 00:01:45,310
I've always really liked Jin Jing.

57
00:01:45,320 --> 00:01:46,590
I think she's

58
00:01:46,600 --> 00:01:48,870
not just funny,
but really emotionally intelligent.

59
00:01:48,880 --> 00:01:52,950
So right from the start today,

60
00:01:52,960 --> 00:01:54,870
we really felt like best friends.

61
00:01:54,880 --> 00:01:57,030
Even our back-and-forth jokes

62
00:01:57,040 --> 00:01:58,590
felt really natural.

63
00:01:58,600 --> 00:02:00,590
Somehow, we just ended up holding hands.

64
00:02:00,600 --> 00:02:01,590
Yeah, we really felt

65
00:02:01,600 --> 00:02:03,350
like best friends and neighbors.

66
00:02:03,360 --> 00:02:05,590
We were totally in character.

67
00:02:05,590 --> 00:02:08,669
When you acted opposite Zhou Keyu,

68
00:02:08,669 --> 00:02:11,160
during the martial arts
matchmaking scene,

69
00:02:11,490 --> 00:02:14,230
was he different
from how you'd imagined him?

70
00:02:16,240 --> 00:02:17,710
I'd seen

71
00:02:17,720 --> 00:02:19,870
Zhou Keyu
in Sniping the Butterfly before.

72
00:02:19,880 --> 00:02:22,870
Honestly, he wasn't that different.

73
00:02:22,880 --> 00:02:23,630
He's just

74
00:02:23,640 --> 00:02:25,990
really sunny and handsome.

75
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:28,590
And during our

76
00:02:28,600 --> 00:02:30,910
rehearsal today, he was really patient.

77
00:02:30,920 --> 00:02:32,150
It was really hot,

78
00:02:32,160 --> 00:02:35,030
but he kept going over

79
00:02:35,040 --> 00:02:35,990
the lines every time.

80
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:36,630
Very professional.

81
00:02:37,360 --> 00:02:40,310
Did any of the other players
stand out to you?

82
00:02:40,800 --> 00:02:42,910
Ning was amazing.

83
00:02:42,920 --> 00:02:44,510
I never expected

84
00:02:44,520 --> 00:02:46,830
Ning to be the one doing the splits.

85
00:02:46,840 --> 00:02:47,590
I'll try.

86
00:02:47,600 --> 00:02:48,510
I don't know.

87
00:02:48,520 --> 00:02:49,510
Lately,

88
00:02:49,520 --> 00:02:53,150
I'm getting a little old
for fancy footwork.

89
00:02:53,160 --> 00:02:53,980
A little farther.

90
00:02:55,470 --> 00:02:56,220
A little farther.

91
00:02:59,440 --> 00:03:00,990
I was totally unprepared for that.

92
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:02,110
At first,

93
00:03:02,120 --> 00:03:04,150
we talked with the directors about

94
00:03:04,160 --> 00:03:05,870
who might actually do the splits

95
00:03:05,880 --> 00:03:08,870
and what we'd do if nobody did.

96
00:03:08,880 --> 00:03:10,670
But the second Ning did it,

97
00:03:10,680 --> 00:03:12,590
I couldn't even control my expression.

98
00:03:12,600 --> 00:03:13,470
I was genuinely shocked.

99
00:03:13,730 --> 00:03:15,770
The fight scenes
were your biggest challenge.

100
00:03:15,770 --> 00:03:16,960
What was

101
00:03:16,960 --> 00:03:18,790
the hardest part?

102
00:03:19,600 --> 00:03:22,750
I wouldn't call it difficult.

103
00:03:22,760 --> 00:03:24,710
I'd say

104
00:03:24,720 --> 00:03:26,790
the tricky part

105
00:03:26,800 --> 00:03:29,070
was keeping my legs stable.

106
00:03:29,080 --> 00:03:30,870
The instructor gave me this move

107
00:03:30,880 --> 00:03:32,110
where I had to spin around,

108
00:03:32,120 --> 00:03:33,710
then hit this cool

109
00:03:33,720 --> 00:03:35,110
final pose.

110
00:03:35,120 --> 00:03:38,150
But during rehearsal yesterday,

111
00:03:38,160 --> 00:03:39,670
I kept falling over.

112
00:03:39,680 --> 00:03:40,950
I just couldn't stay balanced.

113
00:03:40,960 --> 00:03:43,310
But today went pretty well.

114
00:03:43,320 --> 00:03:44,470
I finally nailed it.

115
00:03:44,480 --> 00:03:45,670
Yeah, even I was surprised.

116
00:03:45,680 --> 00:03:47,350
These period shoes I'm wearing

117
00:03:47,360 --> 00:03:49,110
have a bit of a heel.

118
00:03:49,120 --> 00:03:51,950
But today everything went smoothly.

119
00:03:51,960 --> 00:03:52,870
We got it in one take.

120
00:03:52,880 --> 00:03:53,870
Just one take.

121
00:03:53,960 --> 00:03:56,080
Did you prepare
for the fight scenes beforehand?

122
00:03:56,520 --> 00:03:58,670
I took these shoes back
to the hotel yesterday

123
00:03:58,680 --> 00:04:01,230
and kept practicing in my room.

124
00:04:01,240 --> 00:04:02,670
And something

125
00:04:02,680 --> 00:04:03,870
really funny happened.

126
00:04:03,880 --> 00:04:06,070
I didn't have my sword,

127
00:04:06,080 --> 00:04:08,310
so I grabbed this thing in my room.

128
00:04:08,320 --> 00:04:10,430
It was kind of like

129
00:04:10,440 --> 00:04:12,230
one of those hot pot ladles,

130
00:04:12,240 --> 00:04:13,390
made of wood,

131
00:04:13,400 --> 00:04:14,830
like a long wooden ladle.

132
00:04:14,840 --> 00:04:15,630
I used it as a sword

133
00:04:15,640 --> 00:04:17,190
since it was pretty long.

134
00:04:17,200 --> 00:04:18,709
So I practiced with it.

135
00:04:18,720 --> 00:04:20,510
Then, snap!

136
00:04:20,519 --> 00:04:21,990
I kicked it in half.

137
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:23,350
Yeah, and I had to pay

138
00:04:23,360 --> 00:04:25,070
for that ladle.

139
00:04:25,080 --> 00:04:26,550
I never thought I'd break it.

140
00:04:26,560 --> 00:04:29,190
It looked really sturdy.

141
00:04:29,200 --> 00:04:30,710
But while I was practicing,

142
00:04:30,720 --> 00:04:32,270
it just snapped.

143
00:04:32,280 --> 00:04:33,150
So dramatic.

144
00:04:33,160 --> 00:04:34,750
But I thought,

145
00:04:34,760 --> 00:04:36,750
a little drama's good.

146
00:04:36,760 --> 00:04:38,350
It meant today would turn out great.

147
00:04:39,710 --> 00:04:42,330
(He Wenjun as Junzi Ruyu)
From comedian to mystery-show NPC,

148
00:04:42,330 --> 00:04:44,270
how are the two different?

149
00:04:44,640 --> 00:04:45,830
This isn't really acting.

150
00:04:45,840 --> 00:04:47,070
It's more like

151
00:04:47,080 --> 00:04:49,310
somewhere between acting and not acting.

152
00:04:50,120 --> 00:04:51,230
Sometimes you're acting,

153
00:04:51,240 --> 00:04:52,790
then you break character.

154
00:04:52,800 --> 00:04:54,390
It's this gray area

155
00:04:54,400 --> 00:04:57,270
between acting and reality TV.

156
00:04:57,280 --> 00:04:58,830
It's basically

157
00:04:59,720 --> 00:05:03,110
this "gray acting" where you act,
but don't.

158
00:05:03,120 --> 00:05:04,870
You're playing a character,

159
00:05:04,880 --> 00:05:06,870
but your reactions are real too.

160
00:05:08,100 --> 00:05:10,100
Since you're close with Li Fei,

161
00:05:10,100 --> 00:05:12,080
who was an NPC last episode,

162
00:05:12,080 --> 00:05:12,800
before you came,

163
00:05:12,800 --> 00:05:14,900
did he give you any advice?

164
00:05:14,920 --> 00:05:16,590
He told me,

165
00:05:16,600 --> 00:05:17,230
"Just show up."

166
00:05:17,240 --> 00:05:18,430
"It's super easy."

167
00:05:18,440 --> 00:05:20,510
He said it wasn't mentally taxing

168
00:05:20,520 --> 00:05:21,590
and was really chill.

169
00:05:21,600 --> 00:05:22,910
Just show up, film, and leave.

170
00:05:22,920 --> 00:05:23,990
(Totally believed him)
That's what he told me.

171
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:25,110
Now that you're here,

172
00:05:25,120 --> 00:05:26,510
was he telling the truth?

173
00:05:26,520 --> 00:05:27,950
My brain's fried after today.

174
00:05:27,950 --> 00:05:29,260
(Nothing like he said)

175
00:05:29,390 --> 00:05:30,940
It's your first time on The Truth.

176
00:05:30,940 --> 00:05:31,850
After meeting all the players,

177
00:05:31,850 --> 00:05:33,070
did anyone stand out?

178
00:05:33,280 --> 00:05:34,670
I met some of them today.

179
00:05:34,680 --> 00:05:36,070
I've actually worked with Yang Chaoyue

180
00:05:36,080 --> 00:05:38,070
and Jin Jing before.

181
00:05:38,080 --> 00:05:41,670
My first impression
of the four guys was...

182
00:05:42,480 --> 00:05:43,150
huge pecs.

183
00:05:43,150 --> 00:05:43,740
(Seriously shook)

184
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:44,870
When I turned around,

185
00:05:44,880 --> 00:05:46,790
all I saw were pecs in my face.

186
00:05:47,240 --> 00:05:48,230
I only came up to here.

187
00:05:49,520 --> 00:05:50,390
Like four walls.

188
00:05:51,760 --> 00:05:52,830
Four human shields.

189
00:05:53,280 --> 00:05:54,030
(Still shook)
Zhou Keyu stood there

190
00:05:54,040 --> 00:05:54,790
and blocked me completely.

191
00:05:56,400 --> 00:05:57,190
That was my first impression.

192
00:05:57,530 --> 00:05:58,800
You're back on The Truth.

193
00:05:58,800 --> 00:05:59,950
(The Truth Season 2, Episode 1)
How does it feel?

194
00:05:59,950 --> 00:06:01,500
(Cui Shaoyang as Cui Geng)
Anything new this time?

195
00:06:01,500 --> 00:06:02,040
(The Truth Season 2, Episode 5)

196
00:06:02,040 --> 00:06:02,880
Yeah.

197
00:06:02,880 --> 00:06:03,640
(The Truth Season 3, Episode 6)

198
00:06:03,640 --> 00:06:05,910
I'm really happy to be back.

199
00:06:06,560 --> 00:06:08,270
I got another job.

200
00:06:08,280 --> 00:06:10,350
Yeah, I love working on The Truth.

201
00:06:10,920 --> 00:06:11,950
From The Truth 2

202
00:06:11,960 --> 00:06:13,310
(The Truth Season 2, Episode 1)
all the way to The Truth 4,

203
00:06:13,320 --> 00:06:14,110
(The Truth Season 2, Episode 5)
I feel like

204
00:06:14,120 --> 00:06:15,670
I'm playing people from different eras,

205
00:06:15,680 --> 00:06:17,310
(The Truth Season 3, Episode 6)
constantly traveling through time.

206
00:06:17,320 --> 00:06:18,030
It's been really fun.

207
00:06:18,040 --> 00:06:20,070
And I got to see Linghe

208
00:06:20,080 --> 00:06:21,150
and my old friends again.

209
00:06:23,120 --> 00:06:23,870
It feels really different.

210
00:06:24,840 --> 00:06:26,600
How was acting
with Zhang Linghe this time

211
00:06:26,600 --> 00:06:27,720
different from before?

212
00:06:27,720 --> 00:06:28,840
Anything new?

213
00:06:28,840 --> 00:06:29,590
First, I think

214
00:06:29,600 --> 00:06:31,070
he looks really different.

215
00:06:31,080 --> 00:06:33,510
He looks so thin to me.

216
00:06:33,520 --> 00:06:36,030
When we first walked in today,

217
00:06:36,040 --> 00:06:36,670
you know,

218
00:06:36,680 --> 00:06:39,990
I didn't expect him to be that thin.

219
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:40,790
He said

220
00:06:40,800 --> 00:06:42,790
